AGENTS.md:176:                        #   RedisStateStores.redisOrFallback + its native-image metadata.
AGENTS.md:612:**Complete**: 16-byte opcode engine (`pathland-core`), SwiftUI-style view DSL with decoupled chainable modifiers (`pathland-view`), declarative diff-based reactive emission (`pathland-core`), **reactive signals** (`pathland-core::signal` — writable `Signal` values bound to node text/properties, so a signal change re-emits only the bound nodes, reachable from Java via the `pathland_native_signal_*` / `node_bind_*` C ABI), host reader to a native-element description (`pathland-render-gtk`), opcode transport with network-batch encode/decode + time/size batching policy (`pathland-core-transport`), golden conformance vectors (incl. raw-input EVENT and network-batch bytes), typed raw-input event encode/decode, `no_std` builds, zero-alloc steady-state emission, the **bidirectional event ring** (host → guest EVENT opcodes in shared memory, drained by the host via a generic `pathland_native_drain_events` C ABI — the renderer only writes + wakes), the **GTK4 renderer** (`pathland-render-gtk`) with Rust demos that render through it without touching GTK directly, the **native JVM library set** — `pathland-view-core` (Kotlin: open `View` interface + shared value/SPI vocabulary, **Angular-parity signals/computed/effects** with synchronous flush, fine-grained retained-tree emitter with **node-level binding effects**, `PLPL` wire codec, router, cross-platform `StateStore` + **`PersistentState`**) and the opt-in `pathland-native-core` (`dev.pathland.nativecore` — lazy **JNA ring interop** into `libpathland_core`, kept off the server classpath) and the sole JVM authoring DSL `dev.pathland.view.dsl` (SwiftUI-shaped builders, modifier sugar, property-delegate state, navigation/media helpers, styles), `dev.pathland.render.html` (pure-Java port of the Rust HTML renderer; golden-fixture-checked byte-for-byte), the opt-in `pathland-state-redis` (`dev.pathland.state.redis` — Lettuce `RedisStateStore` + `RedisStateStores.redisOrFallback`) — and the **Quarkus demo** (`pathland-quarkus-demo`, a Java host mounting the Kotlin `MusicPlayerView`/`AdView`, plus a Kotlin-only view at `/kotlin`; builds a GraalVM/Mandrel native executable via its Dockerfile), the **desktop demo** (`pathland-desktop-demo`, GTK and Qt), and the **Spring Boot** (`pathland-spring-boot-demo`, a Java host mounting Kotlin views) **SSR + WebSocket demos** with per-window persisted `State` (Redis/in-memory — every browser window/tab gets its own UI model and state scope via a `sessionStorage` window id, so two windows never share a session). **`EVENT_LISTENERS`** (any element emits raw events via a u32 bitmask property) and **`onTapGesture`** (Rust + Kotlin DSL modifier + app-side `TapRecognizer` over the raw pointer events). **Generic input routing** — the emitter returns tap-action / text-input / value-input registries (`RenderResult`), so the host forwards raw `EVENT` batches straight into the bound signals and never reaches into a view's internals. **The media kit** (spec/MEDIA.md) — a non-visual `MEDIA_CONTROLLER` (0x30) state object owning a resource + transport as signals, referenced by a `VIDEO` (0x0A) surface and controlled by the app's own views; **audio has no view**. Implemented across spec, `pathland-core`, the GTK + HTML renderers, the TS DOM client, the Kotlin DSL/emitter, and the Rust DSL/engine (a `MediaController` + `Video` + `attach()`, with string-property signal bindings and a **pinned** controller node id so a `SIZE_THAT_FITS` band swap never restarts playback). **Attributed text** (`SET_ATTRIBUTED_TEXT`) — `AttributedString` model/codec, the shared `pathland-markdown` inline parser (+ `pathland-markdown-capi` for non-JVM hosts; the JVM parser is a pure-Java port), Rust/Kotlin DSL builders, GTK markup, SSR spans/anchors, and DOM-client application. **Built-in Markdown `Text`** — `Text("**hi**")` auto-parses in both DSLs (SwiftUI-like; `markdown = false` / `Text::plain` opt out); plain results keep the compact `SET_TEXT` path. **Topic subscriptions (scoped + global)** — a strongly typed `Topic<T,S>` + `topic(key, subject, initial)` for entity-scoped topics and `Topic.global` + `topic(key, initial)` for app-wide ones in the Kotlin DSL, a per-mount `PathlandSignalHub.publish(topic, subject, value)` / `publish(topic, value)`, and `PathlandSession.submit(...)`: external threads update only the sessions subscribed to that scope, with values applied on the session actor and coalesced latest-wins (docs/external-updates.md). **Tests green across the workspace.**
